{%- comment -%}
  Crazy Deals.

  ── What changed, and why ────────────────────────────────────────────────

  This page was making five claims that were not true of anything.

    · Three countdown timers that restarted on every page load. The old
      initCountdowns took a number of hours and counted down from it, so
      "this week's deals end in 34 hours" was 34 hours away on Monday and
      34 hours away again on Friday. Nothing ever ended.
    · "Only 14 left" with a stock bar fixed at 28%.
    · "sold 62 this week".
    · Five filled stars and "(1,102 reviews)", written into the markup.
    · A Deal of the Week — a named product at AED 209, reduced from AED 380
      — that was a picture and some text, not a product. It linked to the
      catalogue rather than to itself, because there was no itself.

  Those are the false-urgency and bait-and-switch patterns, and the first
  item on the pre-launch compliance checklist is that a storefront carries
  none of them. They are also, separately, bad trade: a timer that resets is
  only persuasive until someone comes back, and the shopper it misleads is
  the one who was ready to buy.

  Everything on the page now comes from real data or is not rendered:

    · The timer counts to a date set in the theme editor. No date, no timer
      and no "ends in" label — not a timer with a default.
    · Deal of the Week is a product picked in the editor. Its price, saving,
      rating and stock are read from that product.
    · "Only N left" appears only when Shopify is tracking inventory and the
      number is genuinely at or under the threshold set below.
    · Stars appear only when the product has reviews.

  The discounts themselves were always real — they come from compare-at
  prices on real products. It was the decoration around them that was not.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign deal_product = section.settings.deal_product
  assign deals_collection = section.settings.deals_collection | default: collections['crazy-deals']

  # The timer is shown only while it is both set and still running. Liquid
  # compares dates as strings here, so both sides go through %s — seconds
  # since the epoch — which compares correctly as numbers.
  assign deal_end = section.settings.deal_end_date | strip
  assign show_timer = false
  if deal_end != blank
    assign ends_at = deal_end | date: '%s' | times: 1
    assign now_at = 'now' | date: '%s' | times: 1
    if ends_at > now_at
      assign show_timer = true
    endif
  endif

  assign dv = deal_product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign deal_save_pct = 0
  if dv.compare_at_price > dv.price
    assign deal_save_pct = dv.compare_at_price | minus: dv.price | times: 100.0 | divided_by: dv.compare_at_price | round
  endif

  # Low stock, only when it is a fact. Shopify reports inventory_quantity as 0
  # when it is not tracking the item at all, which is why "tracked" has to be
  # tested separately — without it every untracked product would claim to be
  # down to its last unit.
  assign low_threshold = section.settings.low_stock_threshold | default: 10 | times: 1
  assign show_low_stock = false
  if dv.inventory_management != blank and dv.inventory_quantity > 0 and dv.inventory_quantity <= low_threshold
    assign show_low_stock = true
  endif

  assign deal_rating = deal_product.metafields.reviews.rating.value.rating
  assign deal_rating_count = deal_product.metafields.reviews.rating_count.value | plus: 0
-%}

    <!-- DEAL HERO -->
    <section class="deal-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">chevron_right</span><span>Crazy Deals</span></div>
        <span class="deal-flag"><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">bolt</span>Limited-Time Offers</span>
        <h1 class="ph-title" style="margin-top:18px">Crazy <em>Deals</em></h1>
        <p class="ph-sub">Serious price drops on 100% authentic fragrances — while stock lasts. New deals every week, dispatched next-day across the UAE. When they're gone, they're gone.</p>
        {%- if show_timer -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            The label and the timer share one wrapper so they disappear
            together when the deadline passes — see initCountdowns.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div data-countdown-scope style="margin-top:30px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap">
            <span style="font-size:.72rem;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:rgba(255,255,255,.6)">This week's deals end in</span>
            <div class="countdown" data-countdown-to="{{ deal_end | escape }}"></div>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- BENEFITS -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="usp-grid fade-up">
          <div class="usp-card"><div class="usp-ic"><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">sell</span></div><h3>Deep Discounts</h3><p>Real markdowns against recommended retail on genuine designer and Arabic-house fragrances — never inflated "was" prices.</p></div>
          <div class="usp-card"><div class="usp-ic"><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">inventory</span></div><h3>Limited Stock</h3><p>Deal quantities are strictly capped. Once a run sells out it's removed — so the price you see is the price while it lasts.</p></div>
          <div class="usp-card"><div class="usp-ic"><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">local_shipping</span></div><h3>Next-Day Delivery</h3><p>Order today, wear it tomorrow. Free UAE delivery over AED {{ settings.free_shipping_threshold | default: '250' }}, with Cash on Delivery available everywhere.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- DEAL OF THE WEEK -->
    {%- comment -%}
      Rendered only when a product has been picked. An empty slot says
      nothing; a slot filled with a product that does not exist says
      something false, which is how this block got here.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if deal_product != blank -%}
    <section class="section alt">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="sec-head"><span class="label">Deal of the Week</span><h2 class="sec-title">The One to <em>Grab First</em></h2></div>
        <div class="deal-spotlight fade-up">
          <div class="ds-media">
            {%- if deal_product.featured_image -%}
              <img src="{{ deal_product.featured_image | image_url: width: 900 }}" alt="{{ deal_product.title | escape }}" width="900" height="900" loading="lazy">
            {%- else -%}
              <img src="{{ 'hero-oud.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="{{ deal_product.title | escape }}" loading="lazy">
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if deal_save_pct > 0 -%}
              <div class="ds-savebadge"><b>-{{ deal_save_pct }}%</b><small>Off</small></div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
          <div class="ds-body">
            {%- if deal_product.vendor != blank -%}<div class="prod-brand">{{ deal_product.vendor }}</div>{%- endif -%}
            <h2 class="sec-title" style="font-size:2rem;margin:4px 0 2px">{{ deal_product.title }}</h2>

            {%- comment -%}
              Stars only with reviews behind them. The old markup drew five
              filled stars and "(1,102 reviews)" on a product that had
              neither — the single most load-bearing claim on the page, and
              entirely invented.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if deal_rating_count > 0 and deal_rating != blank -%}
              <div class="prod-rating">
                {% render 'star-rating', rating: deal_rating %}
                <span style="color:var(--warm);font-size:.82rem">({{ deal_rating_count }} review{% unless deal_rating_count == 1 %}s{% endunless %})</span>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            <div class="ds-price-row">
              <span class="ds-now">{{ dv.price | money_with_currency }}</span>
              {%- if dv.compare_at_price > dv.price -%}
                <span class="ds-was">{{ dv.compare_at_price | money_with_currency }}</span>
                <span class="price-save">Save {{ dv.compare_at_price | minus: dv.price | money_with_currency }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>

            {%- comment -%}
              The stock bar was fixed at 28% regardless of anything. It now
              tracks the real remaining count against the threshold, and both
              it and the line beneath it are absent unless Shopify is
              actually counting this product's units.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if show_low_stock -%}
              {%- assign stock_pct = dv.inventory_quantity | times: 100 | divided_by: low_threshold -%}
              <div class="ds-stock"><i style="width:{{ stock_pct }}%"></i></div>
              <p style="font-size:.8rem;color:var(--warm);margin-bottom:20px"><b style="color:var(--gold-dk)">Only {{ dv.inventory_quantity }} left</b> in stock</p>
            {%- endif -%}

            <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap">
              {%- comment -%}
                Goes to the product. The old button said "Grab This Deal" and
                sent the shopper to the whole catalogue, because the deal it
                described was not a page you could reach.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <a class="btn-g" href="{{ deal_product.url }}"><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">shopping_bag</span>Grab This Deal</a>
              {%- if show_timer -%}
                <div class="countdown compact" data-countdown-to="{{ deal_end | escape }}"></div>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    {%- endif -%}

    <!-- ALL DEALS GRID -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="results-head"><div><span class="label">On Sale Now</span><h2 class="sec-title" style="font-size:2rem">All <em>Crazy Deals</em></h2></div><a class="btn-ghost" href="/collections/all">Shop full catalogue <span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">arrow_forward</span></a></div>
        {%- if deals_collection.products.size > 0 -%}
          <div class="products-grid">{%- for product in deals_collection.products limit: 8 -%}{% render 'product-card', product: product %}{%- endfor -%}</div>
          {%- comment -%}
            "Load More Deals" went to Best Sellers, which is a different set
            of products. It goes to the rest of this collection now.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if deals_collection.products_count > 8 -%}
            <div class="load-more-wrap"><a class="btn-ol" href="{{ deals_collection.url }}">See all {{ deals_collection.products_count }} deals</a></div>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- else -%}
          <div class="products-grid" data-render="products" data-count="8"></div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- TESTIMONIALS -->
    {%- comment -%}
      Real reviews, or no reviews section at all. Judge.me holds this store's
      actual reviews; what used to fill this block was six invented customers
      written into app.js. With none synced the whole section — heading
      included — is absent, rather than a promise of testimonials over a gap.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign tfs_shop_reviews = shop.metafields.judgeme.shop_reviews_count | plus: 0 -%}
    {%- if tfs_shop_reviews > 0 -%}
    <section class="reviews">
      <div class="reviews-inner">
        <div class="reviews-head fade-up"><span class="label">Happy Bargain-Hunters</span><h2 class="sec-title">Great Scents, <em>Great Prices</em></h2></div>
        {% render 'shop-reviews', show: 'carousel' %}
      </div>
    </section>
    {%- endif -%}

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="faq">
      <div class="faq-inner">
        <div class="faq-head fade-up"><span class="label">Your Questions, Answered</span><h2 class="sec-title">Crazy Deals <em>FAQs</em></h2></div>
        <div class="faq-list fade-up">
          <details class="faq-item"><summary class="faq-q">Are Crazy Deals still 100% authentic?<span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">add</span></summary><div class="faq-a">Absolutely. Deal pricing never affects authenticity — every fragrance is genuine, verified-sourced sealed stock, or from our own manufactured brands. Deals are simply overstock, seasonal clearances and negotiated buys we pass on to you.</div></details>
          <details class="faq-item"><summary class="faq-q">Why are some deals limited to a few units?<span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">add</span></summary><div class="faq-a">Deal allocations are genuinely capped by what we've secured at that price. When a run sells out, the deal is removed rather than quietly re-priced — so the discount you see is real.</div></details>
          <details class="faq-item"><summary class="faq-q">Can I return a discounted item?<span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">add</span></summary><div class="faq-a">Deal items carry the same terms as full-price orders: {{ settings.returns_window_days | default: '2' }} days to report anything damaged, defective, incorrect or incomplete, on unused, sealed products. Change-of-mind returns are not accepted on fragrance, discounted or not. Message our team on WhatsApp to arrange a collection.</div></details>
          <details class="faq-item"><summary class="faq-q">How often do new deals drop?<span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">add</span></summary><div class="faq-a">We refresh Crazy Deals weekly, with flash offers in between. Subscribe on WhatsApp or email to be the first to know when new deals go live.</div></details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CLOSING CTA -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container"><div class="cta-band">
        {%- comment -%}
          The flag, the heading and the line beneath them all asserted a
          deadline. With a date set they still do and it is true; without
          one they say what is true either way, which is that stock runs out.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if show_timer -%}
          <span class="deal-flag" style="margin-bottom:14px"><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">timer</span>Ending Soon</span>
          <h2 class="sec-title">Don't Miss Out — <em>Shop Before It's Gone</em></h2>
          <p class="sec-sub">These prices disappear when the timer hits zero or stock runs out — whichever comes first.</p>
          <div data-countdown-scope style="display:flex;justify-content:center;margin:22px 0 26px"><div class="countdown" data-countdown-to="{{ deal_end | escape }}"></div></div>
        {%- else -%}
          <span class="deal-flag" style="margin-bottom:14px"><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">bolt</span>While Stock Lasts</span>
          <h2 class="sec-title">Don't Miss Out — <em>Shop Before It's Gone</em></h2>
          <p class="sec-sub">Deal runs are capped by what we secured at that price. When a run sells out, the deal comes down.</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        <div class="cta-actions">
          <a class="btn-g" href="{{ deals_collection.url | default: '/collections/all' }}"><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">bolt</span>Shop All Deals Now</a>
          <a class="btn-o" href="#" onclick="openReferral();return false">Get Deal Alerts</a>
        </div>
      </div></div>
    </section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Crazy Deals page",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Sale deadline" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "The countdown only ever counts to the moment below. Leave it empty and no timer renders anywhere on the page — which is correct whenever there is no real deadline, and is why there is no default. A timer that restarts on every page load is the false-urgency pattern regulators name first, and it stops working on anyone who visits twice." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "deal_end_date", "label": "Deals end at", "info": "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM in store time, e.g. 2026-10-19 23:59. Clear it when the sale is over — past this moment the timer removes itself." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Deal of the week" },
    { "type": "product", "id": "deal_product", "label": "Featured deal", "info": "Price, saving, rating and stock are all read from this product. Leave empty to hide the whole block." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "low_stock_threshold", "label": "Call stock low at or below", "min": 1, "max": 50, "step": 1, "default": 10, "unit": "u", "info": "\"Only N left\" shows only when Shopify is tracking this product's inventory and the real count is at or under this. Untracked products never show it." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Deals grid" },
    { "type": "collection", "id": "deals_collection", "label": "Collection to show", "info": "Defaults to the Crazy Deals collection." }
  ],
  "presets": [ { "name": "Crazy Deals page" } ]
}
{% endschema %}
